{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 reaper-datasource\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Native tabular-data parsing for REAPER ReaScripts \u8212- spreadsheets and CSV, no backend required. Functions appear in the {\f1 reaper} namespace; all calls are synchronous and return JSON strings.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Parse whole workbooks (.xlsx/.xlsm/.xlsb/.xls/.ods/.csv/.tsv) in one call\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Or open a handle and query sheets, row ranges, and cells incrementally\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Hidden-row detection, delimiter sniffing, unbounded result sizes\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 After installing, run {\f1 reaper.DataSource_OpenDocs()} from any script to open the bundled API reference in your browser.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaSock\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A bridge between REAPER and other programs. ReaSock opens a local WebSocket that speaks JSON-RPC 2.0, so tools outside REAPER can:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Lend} REAPER actions: register entries in the action list that users can bind to keys, menus, and toolbars, and get called when they run\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Tell}: follow transport, project, and selection changes as they happen\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Ask}: read tracks, items, takes, and markers\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Scripts inside REAPER can use the same protocol through ReaSock_Open, ReaSock_Call, and ReaSock_Poll.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b ReaSock_Inspector panel} (needs ReaImGui) shows the project, transport, and selection live, as an example of using ReaSock from a script.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Run {\b ReaSock: Open API documentation} from the Actions list, or call {\f1 reaper.ReaSock_OpenDocs()}, for the full reference.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
